# Contributing

Use issues to describe reproducible problems or proposed changes before large
implementation work.

## Local checks

Run the same checks used by CI before opening a pull request.

{{VERIFIED_SETUP_BUILD_AND_TEST_INSTRUCTIONS}}

## Pull requests

Describe the user-visible change, link relevant issues, and include verification
results. Keep unrelated changes separate.

Use a Conventional Commit PR title, such as `fix: handle an empty configuration`
or `feat(settings): add a reset action`. Mark breaking changes with `!` and
describe the migration in the PR body. Maintainers use squash merges with the
reviewed PR title as the commit subject.

## Releases

{{ACTUAL_RELEASE_AND_VERSIONING_PROCESS}}

For new Release Please setups, maintainers review and merge release PRs. Merging
a release PR isn't evidence that public artifacts or installation have passed
verification.
